  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual claim and visual material",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the false textual claim ('bones of anti-nazi german women still are in the brick ovens on the crematorium') and the visual material of the brick ovens, which together form a misleading historical narrative. The user is implicitly invited to accept or react to this false assertion, which is presented as fact through the juxtaposition of the image and text. There are no explicit deictic pronouns like 'me' or 'you', but the overall intent of the meme is to provoke a reaction from the user by presenting a distorted historical claim.",
